DevOps Engineers What They Actually Do All Day

The results were... eye-opening:

40% of time: Debugging YAML indentation 
25% of time: Googling cryptic error messages
15% of time: Explaining why the deployment failed 
10% of time: Waiting for builds to finish
5% of time: Actually building new features 
5% of time: Pretending Kubernetes makes sense 🤣 

The dirty truth? Most "DevOps" is just "Ops" with extra steps and YAML.

But here's what the top 10% actually spend time on:
- Automating the boring stuff
- Building self-service tools for developers
- Making systems that heal themselves
- Writing docs that don't suck
